---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';

const related = [
  { href: '/journal/brake-pad-sets/', label: 'What comes in a brake pad set?' },
  { href: '/journal/alternator-labels/', label: 'Reading the label on an alternator' },
  { href: '/journal/', label: 'All articles' },
];
---

<Article
  title="Mirror glass or the whole assembly? | Parts Relay"
  description="Describe the damage and equipment so your supplier can quote mirror glass, a cover or the complete assembly."
  heading="Mirror glass or the whole assembly?"
  topic="Parts identification"
  topicHref="/journal/"
  readTime="3 min read"
  relatedHeading="More from the Journal"
  related={related}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    If a repair order says “left mirror,” ask what broke. The shop may need a pane of glass, a
    painted cover, or everything that bolts to the door. That answer changes what the distributor
    looks up.
  </Fragment>
  <div
    slot="cover"
    class="lib-art lib-art-mirror"
    aria-label="Editorial illustration of the glass separated from a left mirror"
    role="img"
  >
    <span>Bodywork</span>
    <i class="lib-shell-shape"></i>
    <i class="lib-glass-shape"></i>
    <b>MIRROR GLASS</b>
  </div>
  <section>
    <h2>Which side of the car?</h2>
    <p>
      Describe left and right from the seat, facing forward. “Driver’s side” can mean different
      things to a supplier working with both left-hand-drive and right-hand-drive vehicles.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="lib-case">
    <h2>What to look up for each repair</h2>
    <p>
      Use the catalogue drawing to see whether the manufacturer lists the damaged piece on its own.
    </p>
    <dl class="lib-evidence">
      <div>
        <dt>Cracked glass</dt>
        <dd>
          For an intact left housing with heated glass, ask the counter to quote the heated pane.
          Check whether that reference includes the backing plate.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Damaged outer cover</dt>
        <dd>
          Ask about the cover for the affected side. Confirm the finish and whether the shop will
          need to have it painted.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Broken mounting base</dt>
        <dd>
          Ask for the complete assembly if that’s how the catalogue supplies the mount. Tell the
          counter which equipment the replacement has to carry.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>What’s still working?</h2>
    <p>
      For cracked glass, find out whether the housing and adjuster survived. Note the heater
      connections and any warning indicator on the glass. For damage to the whole unit, the
      equipment to check may include a folding mechanism or a camera.
    </p>
  </section>
  <p>
    <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/tools/parts-diagrams/">
      Find a component in an exploded view
      <svg
        aria-hidden="true"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.55"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
      >
        <path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" />
      </svg>
    </a>
  </p>
  <p class="lib-product-note">
    Parts Relay finds the parts from a plate or VIN and keeps each search in one queue the whole
    counter can see.
    <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/about/">
      How Parts Relay works
    </a>
  </p>
</Article>
